(1)  201/    1888 :                     
(1)  202/    1888 :                     ; the Nemesis decompressor uses prefix-free codes (no valid code is a prefix of a longer code)
(1)  203/    1888 :                     ; e.g. if 10 is a valid 2-bit code, 110 is a valid 3-bit code but 100 isn't
(1)  204/    1888 :                     ; also, when the actual compressed data is processed the high bit of each code is in bit position 7
(1)  205/    1888 :                     ; so the code needs to be bit-shifted appropriately over here before being used as a code table index
(1)  206/    1888 :                     ; additionally, the code needs multiple entries in the table because no masking is done during compressed data processing
(1)  207/    1888 :                     ; so if 11000 is a valid code then all indices of the form 11000XXX need to have the same entry
(1)  208/    1888 :                     NemBCT_ShortCode:
(1)  209/    1888 : 1018                		move.b	(a0)+,d0			; get code
(1)  210/    188A : E368                		lsl.w	d1,d0				; get index into code table
(1)  211/    188C : D040                		add.w	d0,d0				; shift so that high bit is in bit position 7
(1)  212/    188E : 7A01                		moveq	#1,d5
(1)  213/    1890 : E36D                		lsl.w	d1,d5
(1)  214/    1892 : 5345                		subq.w	#1,d5				; d5 = 2^d1 - 1
(1)  215/    1894 :                     
