(1) 1134/    6320 :                     ScrollHoriz:
(1) 1151/    6320 :                     		; The intent of this code is to make the camera briefly lag behind the
(1) 1152/    6320 :                     		; player right after releasing a spin dash, however it does this by
(1) 1153/    6320 :                     		; simply making the camera use position data from previous frames. This
(1) 1154/    6320 :                     		; means that if the camera had been moving recently enough, then
(1) 1155/    6320 :                     		; releasing a spin dash will cause the camera to jerk around instead of
(1) 1156/    6320 :                     		; remain still. This can be encountered by running into a wall, and
(1) 1157/    6320 :                     		; quickly turning around and spin dashing away. Sonic 3 would have had
(1) 1158/    6320 :                     		; this same issue with the Fire Shield's dash abiliity, but it shoddily
(1) 1159/    6320 :                     		; works around the issue by resetting the old position values to the
(1) 1160/    6320 :                     		; current position (see 'Reset_Player_Position_Array').
